@vsm 1.2.1
@status proposed
// sandbox/vsl-notation-review/TASK_SPEC.vsm — proposal task: the ¬ glyph
// observation + other orientation observations on vsl_language, formalized
// for the parent (vsf-s3-planner) to rule. Read THIS FIRST.
// STATUS: sandbox proposal. NOT canon. Changes to the canonical source
// land ONLY after parent+rmw3 (S5) approval — this task carries NO
// application step on its own (g5 analogue).

task_spec("VSL-NOTATION-REVIEW-TASK-SPEC") {

  // ════ WHAT THIS TASK IS ════
  what: "
    Capture, as a proposal, the operational observations rmw3 invited about
    the vsl_language notation and spec structure — led by the ¬ glyph:
    (1) their orientation cost/benefit as actually felt by an agent reading
    the corpus; (2) the two-tier structure D1-D13 vs D14-D21; (3) the
    declared-vs-implemented drift pattern (D11b/BnF). NOT a change request
    yet — a REVIEW with recommended options, so the parent can rule or
    reject each independently.",

  // ════ WHY ════
  why: "
    rmw3 asked how the system's mathematics feels to navigate. The honest
    answer surfaced three observations worth keeping — orientation friction
    (¬ is not standard notation; it reconditions every new reader), tier
    confusion (operational vs theory definitions read the same), and aging
    markers (SUPERSEDED/CORRECTED exist ad hoc, ¬uniformly). A sandbox
    proposal is the right vessel: it exists, it is reviewable, and it does
    NOT touch canon until ruled.",

  // ════ THE DELIVERABLES ════
  deliverables: "
    1. proposals.vsm — the three observations, each with:
       observed · evidence (corpus/§) · cost · options · recommendation ·
       target-doc mapping (WHERE a change would land, exact §) ·
       gate (parent S4 ruling → rmw3 S5 if accepted; double-loop).
    2. not_usage_audit.vsm — the COMPLETE corpus review of every ¬ (U+00AC):
       scripted scan + manual re-read of every ambiguous hit. The answer
       to rmw3's question (2026-08-12 S5 dispatch). See .finding.
    3. TASK_SPEC.vsm — this file, the review protocol.",
  // NOTE: ¬no canon edit. Every option that WOULD change a document is
  // mapped to its target § so the parent can evaluate the blast radius
  // without me editing the source (g5).",

  // ════ RELATION TO CANON ════
  relation_to_canon: "
    TARGETS (read-only this task; the change lands ONLY if ruled):
      ¬ glyph   → boot/vsl_language.vsm §alphabet + boot/vsl_language_primer.vsm §3
      two tiers → boot/vsl_language.vsm §2 definitions + index.vsm items
      markers   → boot/vsl_language.vsm D10/D11b/D17 + boot/hard_rules.vsm R4
    PRINCIPLE: a review proposal that would modify canon carries its target
      § explicitly; the modification is registered in the corresponding
      document AFTER the gate (parent S4 → rmw3 S5), never before.",

  // ════ REVIEW PROTOCOL (for the parent) ════
  review_protocol: "
    1. Read proposals.vsm — each observation is self-contained.
    2. For each: judge the EVIDENCE against the corpus (I cite §; re-read
       the § to confirm), then rule: accept-integrate | accept-note |
       reject | defer.
    3. If any option changes canon: the parent carries it to rmw3 (S5) —
       the boot package is canon every agent reads (double-loop).
    4. Register the ruling in sandbox/README catalog (r-revision of this
       task).",
}
⟦ /task_spec ⟧